t (y0 + k·h, x0 − k·w) and another at (y0 + k·h, x0 + k·w). This continues until the copies leave the bottom of the grid, and parts outside the grid are clipped.\n\n**Checking against the other pairs.**\n- Pair 3: the 4×2 rectangle at rows 13–16, columns 16–17 produces copies at rows 17–20, columns 14–15 and 18–19. Next come rows 21–24 at columns 12–13 and 20–21, then rows 25–28 at columns 10–11 and 22–23. That matches the listed output objects.\n- The 2×3 rectangle in pair 3 cascades the same way, down to the 2-wide clipped pieces at the left and right edges.\n- In pair 2, three rectangles cascade independently. Where their copies overlap, the result is simply their union, because everything is the same colour on background. This explains the large merged blob.\n\n**Test input.** There are two rectangles:\n- A 4×2 rectangle at rows 8–11, columns 6–7. Its copies sit 4 rows lower each step and 2 columns further out on each side.\n- A 2×4 rectangle at rows 19–20, columns 15–18. Its copies sit 2 rows lower each step and 4 columns further out on each side.\n\nEach rectangle is stamped down until it runs off the bottom, with clipping at the left and right edges. The two cascades are overlaid.\n\n**Construction stages.** The program starts from the input, then completes one rectangle's full cascade per stage and emits the canvas after each.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    out = g.copy()\n    emit(out, \"Start from the input; each solid rectangle will cascade copies diagonally downward.\")\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        h, w = y1 - y0 + 1, x1 - x0 + 1\n        col = o[\"colour\"]\n        k = 1\n        while y0 + k * h < H:\n            ty = y0 + k * h\n            for tx in (x0 - k * w, x0 + k * w):\n                ya, yb = ty, min(H, ty + h)\n                xa, xb = max(0, tx), min(W, tx + w)\n                if xa < xb:\n                    out[ya:yb, xa:xb] = col\n            k += 1\n        emit(out, f\"Rectangle {h}x{w} at ({y0},{x0}): stamped copies one height down and one width left/right per step until leaving the grid.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final: union of all cascades.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each rectangle is stamped down until it runs off the bottom, with clipping at the left and right edges."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Rectangle 2x5 at (9,6): stamped copies one height down and one width left/right per step until leaving the grid."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Rectangle 2x3 at (3,4): stamped copies one height down and one width left/right per step until leaving the grid."}],"boolean":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Where their copies overlap, the result is simply their union, because everything is the same colour on background."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Final: union of all cascades."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Where their copies overlap, the result is simply their union, because everything is the same colour on background."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"8b5ca85affe69acf14747bb9fb71a8d738babbafbd816529f390a49d60a515e9","task_sha256":"cb4ceb96b019072adf34a94cffc60d61f05549a9526f4f9023266431577a2154","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
